      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "REGAL RIPPER (3) was up in trip last time and had a horror outside draw, settling back and wide and never got into the race. Blinkers added, back in trip and this time drawn for a smother stalking a good pace. On the quick back-up with the claim and will be hard to hold out. SOMEWHERE SOON (5) returned with an eye-catching run over 1400m, charging late into fourth. Fitter and will relish the extra ground on the bay to even longer races. NO MANS LAND (8) is a lightly raced galloper who has found the line strongly at the last two. First try this longer trip and drawn for a good run. WINNING ALL ROUND (4) is racing well winning the maiden fresh then runner-up in a Class 1 latest. Fitter again and should appreciate the longer trip. HAMNER SPRINGS (9) was good from a wide gate last time over a little further. Big winner at 1600m the start prior and will give a sight with the light weight.",
